---
id: org.dxos.plugin.crm
name: CrmPlugin
version: 0.1.0
---

A Composer plugin that contributes a **CRM skill** for researching people
and organizations and producing structured Profile documents in the user's
space. v1 is a library-layer plugin only — no UI surfaces. It is deliberately
thin: the heavy lifting (web research, database CRUD, markdown document
creation) is reused from existing `@dxos/assistant-toolkit` skills
(`research`, `database`, `markdown`). plugin-crm contributes CRM-specific
instructions, one relation schema, one image-attachment operation, and a
pluggable research-source contract for future extensions (e.g., a LinkedIn
browser-extension integration).

Given a reference to a `Person`, `Organization`, or an email `Message`, the
skill drives an agent to (a) locate or create the corresponding Person
and Organization ECHO objects, (b) produce a markdown Profile document
following an editable section template, (c) link the Profile to its subject
via a typed `ProfileOf` relation, and (d) attach a best-effort avatar /
company-logo image uploaded to the DXOS image service.

## Extensions

The following extension dialects are used in this document.
Each extension is defined in the Appendix or resolved via its URI.

| Term        | URI                            |
|-------------|--------------------------------|
| `type`      | `org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0`        |
| `feat`      | `org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0`        |
| `test`      | `org.dxos.mdl.test@1.0`        |
| `op`        | `org.dxos.mdl.op@1.0`          |
| `service`   | `org.dxos.mdl.service@1.0`     |
| `skill` | `org.dxos.mdl.skill@1.0`   |
| `op@1.1`    | `org.dxos.mdl.op@1.1`      |
| `flow`      | `org.dxos.mdl.flow@1.0`    |

## Types

```mdl
type ContactExtract
  desc: >
    Structured output of the email-signature extractor utility.
    Pure function; computed from a Message's sender + blocks.
  fields:
    fullName?: string
    email: string
    phone?: string
    orgName?: string               # e.g., "Silverline Partners"
    orgDomain?: string             # e.g., "silverline-partners.example" (from email host)
    locations?: string[]           # e.g., ["New York", "San Francisco"]
    urls?: string[]                # any URLs found in the signature block
    isFreeMailDomain: boolean      # gmail, outlook, icloud, yahoo, ...
```

```mdl
type ProfileOf
  desc: >
    ECHO relation linking a Profile Document to its subject (Person or Organization).
    A single Profile Document may have multiple ProfileOf relations when
    research covers both a Person and their Organization.
    Typename: org.dxos.relation.plugin-crm.profile-of
  fields:
    sources: string[]              # URLs / provider IDs that contributed to the profile
    lastResearchedAt: DateTime     # ISO 8601 UTC timestamp
    summary?: string               # 1–2 sentence abstract of the profile
  relation:
    source: Document               # org.dxos.type.document
    target: Person | Organization  # org.dxos.type.person | org.dxos.type.organization
```

```mdl
type ResearchSource
  desc: >
    Pluggable contract for augmenting the CRM skill with additional
    research tools. Consumers register a ResearchSource; the CRM skill
    picks up its tool definitions at build time. v1 defines the contract
    only — no implementations ship with the plugin. A planned future
    implementation ("LinkedIn via browser extension") will be provided by
    composer-crx.
  fields:
    id: string                     # stable identifier, e.g. "linkedin-crx"
    description: string            # human-readable; referenced in skill instructions
    tools: ToolDefinition[]        # tool defs contributed to the skill
  note: >
    The CRM skill's instructions explicitly mention the sources that
    are registered, so the agent knows to prefer them when appropriate.
```

## Skill

```mdl
skill CrmSkill
  key: org.dxos.skill.crm
  desc: >
    Composes the CRM operations with the web-search, database, and markdown
    skills so an agent can maintain Person/Organization records and enrich
    their Profile documents with researched content.
  depends_on:
    - org.dxos.skill.web-search  # Fetch operation + AnthropicWebSearch (low-level URL fetch + search)
    - org.dxos.skill.database    # object-create, object-update, query, relation-create, load
    - org.dxos.skill.markdown    # create/read/update markdown documents
  contributes:
    - plugin-crm/attach-image
    - plugin-crm/process-mailbox
    - plugin-crm/research-person
    - plugin-crm/research-organization
    - plugin-crm/ProfileOf (schema registration)
    - tools from registered ResearchSource contracts (v1: none)
  instructions: >
    Authored inline in `src/skills/crm/skill.ts`, deliberately thin: entity
    shapes, dedup semantics, and profile structure are owned by the CRM
    operations, so the prose covers only subject resolution, when to prefer
    the operations over ad-hoc object edits, content-enrichment conventions
    for Profile documents, and the reply style.
```

## Operations

```mdl
op attachImage
  key: org.dxos.operation.crm.attachImage
  desc: >
    Downloads an external image URL, re-uploads it to the DXOS image service
    (POST /thumbnail), and stores the returned canonical URL on the subject's
    `image` field. Mirrors the behaviour of composer-crx `createThumbnail`.
  input:
    subject: Ref<Person | Organization>
    url: string                    # external image URL
  output:
    imageUrl: string               # canonical URL returned by the image service
  errors:
    ConfigMissing: imageServiceUrl is not configured
    FetchFailed: unable to download the source image
    UnsupportedContentType: source content-type is not an accepted image format
    UploadFailed: image service rejected the upload
  effects: [http, echo:write]
  requires: [Database, Config, Trace]
  note: >
    Accepted content types: image/jpeg, image/png, image/webp, image/gif.
    SVG is rejected because inline <script> and event handlers make it a
    stored-XSS risk when downstream surfaces embed the image via <object>
    or <iframe>. Content type is inferred from the response or URL
    extension. Failures are returned as structured errors so the agent can
    continue without the image.
```

```mdl
op processMailbox
  key: org.dxos.operation.crm.processMailbox
  desc: >
    Cursored CRM pipeline over a mailbox's message feed. Extracts contacts
    for messages past the persisted feed Cursor using @dxos/extractor-lib
    (same allow-list gate and identity-index dedup as mail sync), records
    provenance on the mailbox, optionally scaffolds a Profile per new
    contact, and advances the cursor page-wise.
  input:
    mailbox: Ref<Mailbox>
    pageSize?: number              # messages per cursor-advance page (default 20)
    research?: boolean             # scaffold a Profile per new contact (default false)
  output:
    processed: number
    contacts: number
    profiles: number
  effects: [echo:write]
  requires: [Database, Operation]
  note: >
    Idempotent: the cursor is a coarse skip keyed on message.created (ECHO's
    native feed cursor is still stubbed) and the space's identity index is
    the precise backstop, so per-item feed-trigger firing is safe — each
    firing catches up and extra firings process nothing. The cursor object
    is tagged with a foreign key (org.dxos.plugin-crm/process-mailbox) so it
    never collides with other feed consumers' cursors (e.g. AnalyzeMailbox).
```

```mdl
op researchPerson
  key: org.dxos.operation.crm.researchPerson
  desc: >
    Deterministic profile scaffolding for a Person: creates a markdown
    Profile skeleton pre-filled from known ECHO data (emails, role,
    organization link), parents it to the subject, and links it via a
    ProfileOf relation. Re-runs refresh lastResearchedAt and never
    regenerate the document body (user/agent-owned after creation).
  input:
    subject: Ref<Person>
  output:
    profile: Ref<Document>
    created: boolean
  effects: [echo:write]
  requires: [Database]
```

```mdl
op researchOrganization
  key: org.dxos.operation.crm.researchOrganization
  desc: >
    Deterministic profile scaffolding for an Organization; mirrors
    researchPerson and additionally lists the space's known people at the
    organization.
  input:
    subject: Ref<Organization>
  output:
    profile: Ref<Document>
    created: boolean
  effects: [echo:write]
  requires: [Database]
```

## Services

```mdl
service ImageService
  desc: >
    DXOS EDGE image service. Accepts a multipart/form-data upload with a
    single `file` field and returns a JSON body containing a canonical
    `url`. Used by composer-crx today and reused verbatim by attach-image.
  loading: lazy
  ops:
    postThumbnail(blob: Blob) → { url: string }
  errors:
    RateLimited: too many requests
    InvalidUpload: the posted file is not an accepted image
  note: >
    Endpoint is `${config.imageServiceUrl}/thumbnail`. The field name `file`
    is shared with composer-crx and should eventually be factored into a
    protocol def.
```

```mdl
service AssistantToolkit
  desc: >
    Reused skills and operations from @dxos/assistant-toolkit.
  loading: eager
  ops:
    webSearch.Fetch(url) → content              # low-level URL fetch
    webSearch.AnthropicWebSearch                # native Anthropic web search tool
    database.objectCreate(typename, fields) → Obj
    database.objectUpdate(ref, fields) → Obj
    database.query(filter) → Obj[]
    database.relationCreate(typename, source, target, fields) → Relation
    database.load(ref) → Obj
    markdown.*                     # create/read/update — Document-level utilities
  note: >
    plugin-crm never reimplements these. The CRM skill declares its
    dependency on the corresponding skills so they are loaded alongside.
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Polymorphic Subject Resolution
  desc: >
    The skill accepts a Ref<Person | Organization | Message> and
    branches deterministically based on the loaded object's typename.
  req F-1.1: Skill instructions describe how to load the subject via database.load.
  req F-1.2: Instructions describe the three branches (Person, Organization, Message).
  req F-1.3:
    when: subject is a Message
    then: agent extracts { fullName, email, phone?, orgName?, orgDomain?, locations? }
          from sender + signature blocks
  req F-1.4:
    when: subject is a Person
    then: agent seeds research from Person.fullName, Person.emails, and Person.organization (if set)
  req F-1.5:
    when: subject is an Organization
    then: agent seeds research from Organization.name and Organization.website
```

```mdl
feat F-2: Deterministic Contact Extraction
  desc: >
    Contact-extraction semantics are owned by @dxos/extractor-lib (shared
    with mail sync and plugin-inbox's extractor operations), not by
    plugin-crm: buildContactFromActor builds the Person, the IdentitySpecs
    dedupe by normalized email / website domain, and shouldExtractContact
    gates extraction with an allow-list (a sender earns a record only when
    outbound or at a known Organization domain; never for
    no-reply/bulk/role senders). The processMailbox operation is
    plugin-crm's surface over that machinery.
  req F-2.1: processMailbox delegates to buildContactFromActor with a run-scoped overlay of the space's identity index.
  req F-2.2: A repeat sender never yields a second Person, whether processed by this operation or by mail sync.
  req F-2.3: Extraction provenance for feed messages is recorded via Mailbox.recordExtraction (feed items cannot be relation endpoints).
  req F-2.4: plugin-crm ships no parallel extraction heuristics of its own.
```

```mdl
feat F-3: Person & Organization Upsert
  desc: >
    The skill's instructions guide the agent to deduplicate by email
    and by organization domain/name before creating new objects.
  req F-3.1:
    when: an email address is known
    then: agent queries existing Person objects for emails containing that address
  req F-3.2:
    when: no matching Person exists
    then: agent creates a new Person with extracted fields via database.objectCreate
  req F-3.3:
    when: a matching Person exists
    then: agent updates it via database.objectUpdate with newly discovered fields (non-destructive)
  req F-3.4:
    when: orgDomain or orgName is known
    then: agent queries existing Organization objects by website or name
  req F-3.5:
    when: no matching Organization exists AND domain is not free-mail
    then: agent creates a new Organization
  req F-3.6:
    when: a Person has an Organization
    then: agent ensures Person.organization references the Organization
```

```mdl
feat F-4: Research & Profile Composition
  desc: >
    Profile structure is deterministic; profile content is agentic. The
    researchPerson / researchOrganization operations scaffold the document
    skeleton (Overview, Details, Organization|People, Key Links, Notes,
    Sources) pre-filled from known ECHO data and create the ProfileOf
    relation; the agent enriches sections in place using the web-search and
    markdown skills.
  req F-4.1: The section template is rendered by the research operations, not prose; the agent extends sections rather than creating parallel documents.
  req F-4.2: Re-running a research operation refreshes ProfileOf.lastResearchedAt and never regenerates the document body.
  req F-4.3: The "Notes" section records disambiguation hints and uncertainty (e.g., free-mail sender, ambiguous name).
  req F-4.4: The "Sources" section lists URLs that contributed to the profile, mirrored into ProfileOf.sources.
```

```mdl
feat F-5: ProfileOf Relation
  desc: >
    A typed relation links the Profile Document to its subject. This is
    the primary mechanism for discovering profiles from a Person or
    Organization.
  req F-5.1: ProfileOf schema is registered into the space's schema registry at plugin init.
  req F-5.2:
    when: a Profile Document is created for a Person
    then: a ProfileOf relation is created with source=Document, target=Person
  req F-5.3:
    when: a Profile Document also covers an Organization
    then: an additional ProfileOf relation is created with target=Organization
  req F-5.4: Relation carries sources[], lastResearchedAt, and summary.
```

```mdl
feat F-6: Image Attachment
  desc: >
    Best-effort avatar / logo retrieval. The agent finds candidate URLs via
    the existing fetch_url / web search tools; plugin-crm uploads them to
    the DXOS image service and writes the canonical URL onto the ECHO
    object.
  req F-6.1: attachImage operation uploads via POST /thumbnail and writes the result URL to subject.image.
  req F-6.2: imageServiceUrl is read from @dxos/config at invocation time.
  req F-6.3:
    when: imageServiceUrl is not configured
    then: operation returns ConfigMissing error; agent continues without image
  req F-6.4:
    when: image upload fails
    then: operation returns a structured error; subject.image is not modified
  req F-6.5: No fallback search path inside attachImage — the agent is responsible for supplying the URL.
```

```mdl
feat F-7: Pluggable Research Sources
  desc: >
    Future sources (notably LinkedIn via browser extension) will register
    additional tools into the CRM skill. v1 defines the contract but
    ships no implementations.
  req F-7.1: ResearchSource TypeScript interface is exported from src/sources.
  req F-7.2: The CRM skill picks up registered sources' tools at skill.make() time.
  req F-7.3: Skill instructions enumerate the currently-registered sources by id + description so the agent knows what is available.
  req F-7.4: No ResearchSource is bundled in v1; composer-crx will ship the first one in a later PR.
```

```mdl
feat F-8: Configuration Surface (deferred)
  desc: >
    Per-space CrmSettings ECHO type is planned but not implemented in v1.
    v1 relies on @dxos/config for imageServiceUrl and uses only no-auth
    public endpoints for search (inherited from the web-search skill).
  req F-8.1: v1 does NOT ship a CrmSettings schema.
  req F-8.2: Design allows adding CrmSettings later without breaking API — the attachImage operation reads from Config for now.
  req F-8.3: No API keys are required to run v1.
```

```mdl
feat F-9: CRM Navigation Section
  desc: >
    A top-level "CRM" group in the nav tree surfaces the space's Organizations
    and People as plain nodes. Selecting a node opens a generic collection
    article that lists every object of the type, with a toolbar toggle between
    a card (masonry) layout and a schema-derived table.
  req F-9.1: A CRM group node (GraphPath.GroupTypes.crm) is contributed per space and hidden when it has no children.
  req F-9.2: Organizations and People nodes appear under the group only when the space contains objects of that type, mirroring the Database section's natural type folders.
  req F-9.3: Selecting a node opens plugin-space's generic TypeArticle for the type; CRM contributes no article surface of its own.
  req F-9.4: TypeArticle offers a Cards (masonry) and Table (DynamicTable) layout switch; selecting an item opens it as a sibling plank.
```

## Acceptance

```mdl
test T-1: ProcessMailbox — gated extraction over the fixture mailbox
  given: a Mailbox whose feed carries the three email fixtures with distinct timestamps, and
         Organizations seeded for the two corporate .example domains
  when: ProcessMailbox({ mailbox }) is invoked
  then:
    - Persons exist for the two corporate senders, each linked to its Organization
    - NO Person exists for the freemail sender (allow-list gate)
    - Mailbox.extracted records the contact id per corporate message
    - the feed Cursor (tagged org.dxos.plugin-crm/process-mailbox) advanced to the newest message
```

```mdl
test T-2: ProcessMailbox — idempotent and incremental
  given: the state after T-1
  when: ProcessMailbox is re-invoked, then two new messages (one repeat sender, one new sender at a
        known Organization) are appended and it is invoked again
  then:
    - the re-run creates nothing (cursor + identity index)
    - the incremental run creates exactly one Person (the new sender); the repeat sender is deduplicated
```

```mdl
test T-3: ProcessMailbox — research chain
  given: the fixture mailbox from T-1
  when: ProcessMailbox({ mailbox, research: true }) is invoked twice
  then:
    - the first run scaffolds one Profile document + ProfileOf relation per new contact
    - the second run creates no additional profiles or relations
```

```mdl
test T-4: Full-loop playground — corporate short signature (tuning)
  given: a space with the corporate-short email inserted as a Message, memoized LLM, stubbed attachImage, stubbed search
  when: the CRM skill is invoked with the Message ref
  then:
    - a Person exists whose emails contains "padebayo@ventura-advisors.example"
    - an Organization exists whose website ends with "ventura-advisors.example" OR whose name contains "Ventura Advisors"
    - Person.organization references the Organization
    - a Document exists whose content contains "## Overview" and "## Sources"
    - a ProfileOf relation exists with source=Document, target=Person
    - a ProfileOf relation exists with source=Document, target=Organization
```

```mdl
test T-5: Full-loop playground — free-mail personal contact
  given: a space with the freemail-personal email inserted as a Message, memoized LLM, stubbed attachImage, stubbed search
  when: the CRM skill is invoked with the Message ref
  then:
    - a Person exists whose emails contains "riley.nakamura@gmail.com"
    - NO Organization has been created solely because of the sender domain
    - the Profile Document's Notes section mentions any former affiliations surfaced in the message body
    - a ProfileOf relation exists with source=Document, target=Person
```

```mdl
test T-6: Full-loop playground — corporate rich signature
  given: a space with the corporate-rich-signature email inserted as a Message, memoized LLM, stubbed attachImage, stubbed search
  when: the CRM skill is invoked with the Message ref
  then:
    - a Person exists whose emails contains "Saskia.Volkov@silverline-partners.example"
    - an Organization exists whose website ends with "silverline-partners.example" OR whose name contains "Silverline Partners"
    - Organization.location or the Profile Document mentions at least one office city
    - a Document exists following the section template
    - ProfileOf relations exist for both Person and Organization
```

```mdl
test T-7: attachImage — success path
  given: imageServiceUrl is configured; the mock image service returns { url: "https://images.dxos.org/abc" };
         a Person exists with no image
  when: attachImage({ subject: personRef, url: "https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/00000000000000000000000000000000?d=identicon" }) is called
  then:
    - the mock image service received a multipart POST with field "file"
    - Person.image === "https://images.dxos.org/abc"
    - operation output.imageUrl === "https://images.dxos.org/abc"
```

```mdl
test T-8: attachImage — config missing
  given: imageServiceUrl is not configured in @dxos/config
  when: attachImage({ subject: personRef, url: "https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/00000000000000000000000000000000?d=identicon" }) is called
  then:
    - operation returns a structured error tagged ConfigMissing
    - Person.image is unchanged
    - the agent can continue without aborting the run
```

```mdl
test T-9: Graduation — assistant-e2e suite
  given: stable memoized fixtures in packages/core/assistant-e2e/src/testing/crm/fixtures/
  when: CI runs the assistant-e2e test suite
  then:
    - the 3 email fixtures produce the same Person / Organization / Document / ProfileOf graph as the playground tests
    - assertions are tight (exact field values, not substring matches)
  tags: [deferred, post-tuning]
```

---

## Design Notes

### Composition over duplication

plugin-crm is a thin composition layer with a deterministic core. Structural
work — contact extraction, dedup, cursoring, profile scaffolding — is done by
typed operations that compose existing machinery (`@dxos/extractor-lib` for
gate/identity/contact building, `@dxos/link` for the durable feed cursor)
rather than reimplementing it or describing it in prose. Content work — web
research, dossier writing — remains agent-orchestrated through the
`web-search`, `database`, and `markdown` skills from
`@dxos/assistant-toolkit`. This means:

- No `search_web` / `fetch_url` tools of plugin-crm's own; enrichment composes existing skills.
- The trigger loop is deterministic: routines bind `process-mailbox` directly, so no model sits between trigger and operation.
- Tuning structural behaviour is a code change with deterministic tests; tuning content behaviour is a prompt change on the (thin) skill instructions.

### LinkedIn / browser extension seam

LinkedIn is out of scope for v1 code. The `ResearchSource` TypeScript interface
is defined in `src/sources/research-source.ts`, and the skill's `make()`
function iterates over any registered sources and includes their tools in the
skill's tool list. No sources are registered by default. The planned
future implementation will live in `composer-crx` and communicate with the
user's authenticated LinkedIn session via the browser.

### Image attachment — no fallback search

`attach-image` does not itself search for candidate images. The agent finds
them (favicon, OG image, public Gravatar, company-website logo) via the
web-search skill's `Fetch` operation and `AnthropicWebSearch` tool, then
passes the URL to `attach-image`. This keeps the operation small,
single-purpose, and mockable in tests.

### Extraction gate

Sender gating is owned by `shouldExtractContact` in `@dxos/extractor-lib` — an
allow-list (outbound sender, or domain matches a known Organization; never
no-reply/bulk/role mail), shared verbatim with mail sync. This both prevents a
"Gmail" Organization from a free-mail sender and prevents automated senders
from filling the space with contacts nobody will look at. Deterministic
Organization creation from unknown domains is deliberately withheld pending
the allow-list rework (sent-mail recipients; tracked in the mailbox-research
project).

### Profile section template

The section template is rendered by `renderProfile` in
`src/operations/research.ts` (Overview, Details, Organization|People, Key
Links, Notes, Sources). The document body is user/agent-owned after creation:
re-running a research operation refreshes provenance, never content.

### Testing strategy

Three layers:

1. **Operation tests** (`src/operations/{research,process-mailbox}.test.ts`) — deterministic, CI-on-by-default: the fixture-driven feed → cursor → contact → profile chain, idempotency, and the extraction gate.
2. **Template tests** (`src/templates/*.test.ts`) — scaffold shape of the project/automation templates, including the runnable + feed-trigger wiring.
3. **Graded eval** (`packages/core/compute/assistant-evals/src/evals/crm-mailbox.eval.ts`) — the agentic enrichment path, scored with deterministic DB-effect assertions plus an LLM accuracy judge.

### Out of scope for v1

- Settings panel (no CrmSettings surface).
- `CrmSettings` ECHO type (planned; see F-8).
- Any ResearchSource implementation, including LinkedIn.
- API-keyed search providers (Tavily, Brave, Google CSE, Clearbit, etc.).
- Deduping of multiple Person matches by fuzzy-name — v1 updates the best match or asks the user.
- Image-quality heuristics — v1 accepts whatever candidate URL the agent supplies.

---

## QA

Executable flows. Each step carries a human instruction (`do`) and, where the step maps to an
invocable operation, an agent binding (`invoke`). Report failures by flow and step number.

plugin-crm is a library-layer plugin with no UI surfaces (see the document intro) — every step is
driven through the skill's operations, so a "human" run means a person asking the assistant to do
these things in chat, not a navtree gesture. `actors: agent` below reflects that every step has a
real `invoke`.

```mdl
flow QA-1: Research a Person end to end
  desc: The core CRM round-trip — create a Person, scaffold and link its Profile, read it back.
  actors: agent
  covers: [F-1.4, F-4.1, F-5.1, F-5.2, T-4]
  status: unverified
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open
    - no Person named "QA Contact" exists — ABORT rather than reusing one this flow did not create
  test:
    - name: Create the Person
      do: Ask the assistant to add a new contact named "QA Contact" with email "qa.contact@example.com".
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.addObject { object: { "@type": "org.dxos.type.person", fullName: "QA Contact", emails: ["qa.contact@example.com"] } }
      capture: created
      expect: a Person named "QA Contact" now exists in the space
      assert: return !!$created.object
    - name: Research the Person
      do: Ask the assistant to research this contact and produce a profile.
      invoke: [op:researchPerson] { subject: $created.object }
      capture: researched
      expect: a Profile document is created, pre-filled with the known email, and linked to the Person via a ProfileOf relation
      assert: return !!$researched.profile && $researched.created === true
      note: |
        Coalesced with the previous step — `created.object` is live and cannot cross a snippet
        boundary.
    - name: Re-run research is idempotent
      do: Ask the assistant to research the same contact again.
      invoke: [op:researchPerson] { subject: $created.object }
      expect: the same Profile document is returned, not a second one, and only lastResearchedAt changes
      assert: return $result.profile.id === $researched.profile.id && $result.created === false
  after:
    - name: Delete the Person and its Profile
      do: Ask the assistant to remove the "QA Contact" person and its profile document.
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.removeObjects { objects: [$created.object, $researched.profile] }
      expect: neither the Person nor its Profile document exists in the space any more
      assert: |
        return !(await space.db.query(dxos.Filter.everything()).run()).objects
          .some((o) => o.id === $created.object.id || o.id === $researched.profile.id);
```

```mdl
flow QA-2: Attach an image to a Person
  desc: The image-attachment path — a candidate URL is downloaded, re-hosted, and written to `image`.
  actors: agent
  covers: [F-6.1, F-6.2, T-7]
  status: unverified
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open
    - imageServiceUrl is configured for the runtime — otherwise this flow's test step returns
      ConfigMissing and should be re-run once configured, not treated as a defect
    - no Person named "QA Avatar Contact" exists — ABORT rather than reusing one this flow did not
      create
  test:
    - name: Create the Person
      do: Ask the assistant to add a new contact named "QA Avatar Contact".
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.addObject { object: { "@type": "org.dxos.type.person", fullName: "QA Avatar Contact" } }
      capture: created
      expect: a Person named "QA Avatar Contact" now exists with no image
      assert: return !!$created.object && !$created.object.image
    - name: Attach an avatar
      do: Ask the assistant to attach this avatar URL to the contact — "https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/00000000000000000000000000000000?d=identicon".
      invoke: [op:attachImage] { subject: $created.object, url: "https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/00000000000000000000000000000000?d=identicon" }
      expect: the Person's `image` field is a canonical URL from the DXOS image service
      assert: return typeof $result.imageUrl === 'string' && $created.object.image === $result.imageUrl
  after:
    - name: Delete the Person
      do: Ask the assistant to remove "QA Avatar Contact".
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.removeObjects { objects: [$created.object] }
      expect: the Person no longer exists in the space
```

---

## Appendix: Extension Definitions

Extension block types used in this document. Types not redefined here (`type`,
`feat`, `test`, `op`, `service`) follow the definitions in the shared DXOS
MDL extension library (see `packages/plugins/plugin-discord/PLUGIN.mdl`
appendix for reference).

```mdl
ext skill
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.skill@1.0
  desc: >
    A named skill declaration describing its key, dependencies on other
    skills, its contributed operations/schemas, and a prose summary of
    its instructions. The skill's actual instruction text lives in
    source (src/skills/<name>/skill.ts) and is out of scope for
    this document's extension schema.
  fields:
    key: string                  # skill identifier (e.g. org.dxos.skill.crm)
    desc?: Prose
    depends_on?: string[]        # other skill keys this skill composes with
    contributes?: string[]       # operations / schemas introduced by this skill
    instructions?: Prose         # summary; authoritative text lives in code
```
